# =============================================================================
# Environment Variables Template for Basic LangChain Examples
# =============================================================================
#
# PURPOSE:
# This file serves as a template for configuring environment variables required
# by the basic LangChain chain examples in this directory.
#
# SETUP INSTRUCTIONS:
# 1. Copy this file to create your local configuration:
#    cp .env.example .env
#
# 2. Replace all placeholder values with your actual API keys and credentials
#
# 3. The .env file is already in .gitignore and will NOT be committed to version
#    control. The .env.example file (this template) is safe to commit.
#
# HOW TO OBTAIN API KEYS:
# - OpenAI API Key: Sign up at https://platform.openai.com/account/api-keys
#   * Create a new secret key
#   * Copy the key immediately (it won't be shown again)
#   * Typical format: sk-proj-...
#
# - LangSmith API Key (optional): Sign up at https://smith.langchain.com/
#   * Navigate to Settings > API Keys
#   * Create a new API key for tracing and monitoring
#
# SECURITY WARNING:
# ⚠️  NEVER commit your .env file with real credentials to version control!
# ⚠️  Keep your API keys secure and do not share them publicly
# ⚠️  Rotate keys immediately if accidentally exposed
# ⚠️  Use environment-specific keys (development vs production)
#
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OpenAI Configuration (REQUIRED)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required by: All basic chain examples
# The OpenAI API key is necessary for accessing OpenAI's language models
# (GPT-3.5, GPT-4, etc.) used throughout the basic examples.

# Your OpenAI API key - REQUIRED for all examples to run
# Obtain from: https://platform.openai.com/account/api-keys
OPENAI_API_KEY=your-openai-api-key-here

# Optional: Specify which OpenAI model to use
# Default: gpt-3.5-turbo (cost-effective for testing)
# Alternatives: gpt-4, gpt-4-turbo-preview (more capable, higher cost)
OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-3.5-turbo

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LangSmith Tracing Configuration (OPTIONAL)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LangSmith provides observability, debugging, and monitoring for LangChain
# applications. Enable these settings to trace chain executions and debug
# issues more effectively.
#
# Useful for: Understanding chain execution flow, debugging failures, and
# monitoring token usage
#
# Setup: Uncomment the variables below and add your LangSmith credentials

# Enable LangSmith tracing (set to "true" to enable)
# LANGCHAIN_TRACING_V2=false

# Your LangSmith API key
# Obtain from: https://smith.langchain.com/ (Settings > API Keys)
# LANGCHAIN_API_KEY=your-langsmith-api-key-here

# LangSmith project name (organizes your traces)
# You can use different project names for different experiments
# LANGCHAIN_PROJECT=basic-chains-examples

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Example-Specific Requirements
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# simple_llm_chain.py:
#   - Requires: OPENAI_API_KEY
#   - Optional: OPENAI_MODEL, LangSmith tracing
#   - Description: Minimal LLM chain demonstrating basic invoke() usage
#
# prompt_template_chain.py:
#   - Requires: OPENAI_API_KEY
#   - Optional: OPENAI_MODEL, LangSmith tracing
#   - Description: PromptTemplate + LLM composition with variable substitution
#
# lcel_basic_composition.py:
#   - Requires: OPENAI_API_KEY
#   - Optional: OPENAI_MODEL, LangSmith tracing
#   - Description: Simple LCEL pipe composition (prompt | model | parser)
#
# sequential_chain.py:
#   - Requires: OPENAI_API_KEY
#   - Optional: OPENAI_MODEL, LangSmith tracing
#   - Description: SequentialChain with multiple steps demonstrating data flow
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Additional Notes
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# - All examples gracefully handle missing API keys with informative error
#   messages guiding you to this configuration file
#
# - For production use, consider using secret management services like:
#   * AWS Secrets Manager
#   * Azure Key Vault
#   * HashiCorp Vault
#   * Environment-specific CI/CD secrets
#
# - Monitor your API usage and costs at: https://platform.openai.com/usage
#
# - Rate limits apply to OpenAI API keys. See:
#   https://platform.openai.com/docs/guides/rate-limits
#
# =============================================================================
